WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
At the start of 2024,

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.630
the UK had 5.5 million
private sector businesses.

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.600
99.2 per cent of them were small,

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.800
with fewer than 50 employees.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.170
And 74 per cent employed no
one at all except the owners.

6
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.620
Yet a few firms grow into giants,

7
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.030
with branches everywhere
and rivals swallowed up.

8
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.680
So why do a few firms grow huge,

9
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.910
while most firms stay
small all their lives?

10
00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.550
In this mission, you'll see
the two ways a firm can grow:

11
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.940
from the inside, or by
joining another firm.

12
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.000
Then you'll work out what
growing bigger does to the cost

13
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.570
of every loaf a bakery makes.

14
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.250
Your mission: find out
what holds most firms back,

15
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.370
and what changes when one grows.
